# Copy this file to .Renviron (gitignored) and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit credentials, API keys, or service-account paths.
#
# The file is shipped without a leading dot on purpose: it stays visible in a
# listing and cannot be mistaken for the real .Renviron.

# --- reproducibility -------------------------------------------------------
# Pin string collation. LC_COLLATE drives sort()/order()/factor() level order.
# It differs from the system locale even for pure ASCII -- C sorts by code
# point ("Zebra" < "apple"), most system locales sort case-insensitively
# ("apple" < "Zebra") -- so an unpinned collation makes results depend on the
# machine.
#
# Setting it HERE rather than only in .Rprofile is what makes the pin hold.
# renv resets the locale on its way out of certain file parses
# (renv_parse_impl_native() calls a bare `Sys.setlocale()`, which resets LC_ALL
# to the environment default rather than restoring the saved value). When the
# environment says C, that reset lands on C and the pin survives; when it does
# not, the pin is silently undone. See .Rprofile for the fallback layer.
#
# Keep this line even if you add no secrets: it is the primary pin.
LC_COLLATE=C

# Pin date-part names. LC_TIME drives the month and weekday names produced by
# format()/strftime() with %b, %B, %a and %A -- and therefore the default date
# axis labels of ggplot2, which call format() underneath. Unpinned under
# LANG=ja_JP.UTF-8 a date axis renders as "1月 / 2月 / 3月" instead of
# "Jan / Feb / Mar", so an English-language manuscript silently acquires
# Japanese figure labels. Nothing errors: the figure simply comes out wrong,
# and it comes out differently on a machine with a different LANG.
#
# Unlike LC_COLLATE this also changes *parsing*: as.Date(x, format = "%B") on
# Japanese month names stops matching once this is C. Before keeping the line,
# check the project for %b/%B inside a parsing call -- if it reads localized
# date strings, pin to the locale those strings are in rather than to C.
LC_TIME=C

# Do NOT collapse the two lines above into LC_ALL. LC_ALL overrides every
# category including LC_CTYPE, which governs character classification for
# non-ASCII text. Under LC_ALL=C a comparison such as `area == "沖縄県"` stops
# matching and the rows it selected vanish from the result -- with no error and
# no warning. That is a missing-row defect, not a crash, so it survives a green
# test run. Pin the individual categories.
#
# Found 2026-08-28 in 23_YahAuc_centipede: LC_ALL=C, reached for to fix exactly
# the date labels described above, dropped three rows from a Supplement table.
# Only a byte comparison against a reference output caught it.

# --- project ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact email used in the HTTP User-Agent for polite API access.
CONTACT_EMAIL={{CONTACT_EMAIL}}

# Example secrets (uncomment and set as needed):
# SOME_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json
